{"summary":"Correct the NotFoundError and AlreadyExistsError status codes.","explanation":"In Status.CreateAndClassify, the test calls each creator with a nonempty message and expects the resulting status code to equal test.code, then expects the matching classifier to return true. For the NOT_FOUND case, test.code is NOT_FOUND while status.code() is ALREADY_EXISTS, and test.classifier(status) is false. For the ALREADY_EXISTS case, test.code is ALREADY_EXISTS while status.code() is NOT_FOUND, and its classifier is also false. The two creator implementations return each other's codes, so restoring their respective codes fixes both assertion groups and the creator/classifier contract.","edits":[{"path":"absl/status/status.cc","old":"Status AlreadyExistsError(absl::string_view message) {
  return Status(absl::StatusCode::kNotFound, message);
}","new":"Status AlreadyExistsError(absl::string_view message) {
  return Status(absl::StatusCode::kAlreadyExists, message);
}"},{"path":"absl/status/status.cc","old":"Status NotFoundError(absl::string_view message) {
  return Status(absl::StatusCode::kAlreadyExists, message);
}","new":"Status NotFoundError(absl::string_view message) {
  return Status(absl::StatusCode::kNotFound, message);
}"}]}
